  "details": "Bug TLDR: When avatar culling is on, it still shows a light thats on the avatar, and when close, the light isnt even on.\n\n(suspect avatar goes into the state it was in before entering Unity play mode, meaning if that light wasnt hidden in the project, it returns to this state and turns it on when culled?)\n\n1 - Put on avatar culling around avatar with a light\n\n2 - Light stays on\n\nWhat should happen?\n\nThe light should be disabled, especially when lights are such a heavy performance thing. This is also a major issue as you can see in the video, since they didnt even have that light toggle on. Which means if an avatar is culled with a TON of lights that a user isnt using, it may turn on all those lights and lag a player, when the purpose of culling is to help reduce lag.",
